        "summary": "Dc susceptibility of the 1D [Gd2Cu2]n chain is consistent with weak overall antiferromagnetism plus a weak ferromagnetic contribution that slightly raises χMT at intermediate T. Magnetization at 1.8 K/70 kG is 15.7 Nβ. Significant magnetocaloric effect: −ΔSm max = 25.7 J kg−1 K−1 at 2.4 K for ΔH = 70 kG (55.7% of the uncoupled SRln(2S+1) limit of 46.1 J kg−1 K−1).",
