        "procedure": "Method A: A mixture of picolinaldehyde (0.4 mmol), trimethylacetic acid (0.8 mmol), Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.2 mmol), Cu(NO3)2·3H2O (0.4 mmol) and then triethylamine (1.0 mmol) in MeCN/MeOH (5 mL/5 mL) was stirred for 10 min, yielding a blue solution. The solution was filtered and the filtrate evaporated; blue crystals suitable for diffraction formed after several days (10% yield based on picolinaldehyde). Purple crystals of [CuII(L2)2] also formed. Method B: A mixture of 2-pyridinylmethanol (1.0 mmol), trimethylacetic acid (2.0 mmol), Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.5 mmol), Cu(NO3)2·3H2O (1.0 mmol) and then triethylamine (3.0 mmol) in MeCN (10 mL) was stirred for 10 min, filtered, and evaporated; blue crystals formed after several days (20% yield based on 2-pyridinylmethanol).",
